<title>JAPAN: Japan Aug green coffee imports down 2.05 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Aug green coffee imports down 2.05 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports in August totalled 30,626 tonnes, down 2.05 percent from 31,269 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Monday.</p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee amounted to 397 tonnes in August against 172 tonnes the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The breakdown is as follows (in tonnes)</p>
<p>		   Aug 96	   July 96	  Aug 95</p>
<p> Total	   30,626	   29,355	   31,269</p>
<p> Indonesia	6,302	    6,480	    6,815</p>
<p> Colombia	 6,166	    4,865	    4,070</p>
<p> Brazil	   4,688	    4,442	    5,499</p>
<p> Honduras	 1,779	    1,662	    1,385</p>
<p> Guatemala	1,605	    1,798	    1,382</p>
<p>Cumulative green coffee imports in the first eight months of 1996 were 213,462 tonnes against 211,061 tonnes in the same period of the previous year.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Aug 96	 July 96	   Aug 95</p>
<p> Roasted	   397	     268		172</p>
</text>
